Sooner or later I need to ask about the issue of dynamic linking and
I guess this is an opportunity since Mat talked about it in a very
special case.  But my question is more *general*.

Currently, we make libstan.a and libstanc.a.  However, by default, every
linked object used in R I saw is share objects (*.so files under linux).  By default, R
uses and compiles (by R CMD SHLIB) *.so files.  So I guess it is better
to have libstan.so and libstanc.so (or in the end, depending on how we
package RStan, we might have to have them as *.so files).

So is that generally an issue for us?  I guess it shouldn't be.

--
JIqiang

