Wow, I'm surprised the heap is that much slower.  Are you just timing the computation or are you including the memory allocation in the costs as well?

alloca() will dynamically allocate memory on the stack which will be freed when the calling function exits.  You could use this to initialize a block of memory to a runtime configurable but fixed size.  However that's a bit ugly...

Cheers,
Marcus

