Right, there's no need for libstan to be a shared object—the necessary
object code will be pulled out of libstan.a and into the shared object
that dyn.load() loads. In fact, it's simpler this way, since otherwise
we'd have to worry about R being able to find both libstan.so and the
compiled model.

