The command-line option would need to
be given to stanc, as the size would need to
go into the C++ code generated for the model
so that it's available at compile time.

I haven't looked at other platforms/compilers,
but I'm guessing at least the main trend's
going to be the same everywhere.  There's
an indirection in getting things out of the
heap that's not there with the array.

I'm about to grab a latter gcc so that I can
evaluate some threading behavior.  Do people
really care about other platforms? :-)  I'm
really wishing we could've targeted one OS
and one compiler -- this whole project would be
so much simpler.

I'll get a test together and send it to you
if you wouldn't mind running it.

I'm going to try to change everything to
pointer access and pointer arithmetic and
see if that helps.  And aggregate the nodes
and edges of the expression graph into structs
so that there's half as many indexings.

- Bob

