There is one moderately elegant solution I just thought of.  If you have two code paths available, one using a fixed size and another which uses a vector (or some other form of dynamically growing allocation), which can selected at compile time you can:

1) parse and compile the model with dynamic allocation,
2) run a single gradient evaluation and record the number of entries used, and then
2) recompile the model with fixed sized based on the pilot run.

This is obviously not perfect, as it requires a data file at model compile time, but it could be an option for "advanced model optimization..."

