In Ye Olde Fortran, 2**4 is what would now
be written in C++ as std::pow(2,4).

The power operator notation's recognized by R,
too:

 > 2**4
[1] 16
 > 2^4
[1] 16
 > pow(2,4)
Error: could not find function "pow"

Don't worry -- we'll use ^ in Stan when
I get around to adding it.

- Bob

