Thanks for the note.  You were right that the
problem was consuming 'l' too eagerly.  I just
pushed a patch that requires the 'l'/'L' to be
adjacent.

- Bob

On 6/26/12 10:51 PM, Marcus Brubaker wrote:
> Just a quick note, I've stumbled on a bug in the data file format parsing.  In particular, if you have something like
> the following:
>
> foo <- 4
> loo <- 10
>
> the variable loo will not get parsed correctly.  Rather it will get parsed as "oo".  The beginning 'l' will be dropped.
> This is probably due to the logic which is trying to parse the number 4 on the previous line and recognizes a trailing l
> or L.  Not sure of the correct fix here as I don't really know that code at all and I need to sign off but wanted to
> alert the media, so to speak.
>
> Cheers,
> Marcus

